-- title:
--   Linear raw broad-pool supply for every active rough label
-- statement:
--   Fix natural $W,K$ and real $c>0$, $\delta_*>0$. For all sufficiently large $n$, every complete rough label $r$ at cutoff $y(n)$ satisfying the source's intrinsic active nonexceptional condition at $(n,\delta_*)$ has
--   $$|\mathcal B_{W,K}(n,h_c(n),y(n);r)|\ge d_W^{\rm broad}\lfloor n/r\rfloor,$$
--   where $\mathcal B$ is the canonical raw broad correction pool, $h_c(n)$ is the upper tail length and $d_W^{\rm broad}>0$ is the canonical raw-pool density. The eventual threshold is uniform over all such labels.
--
--   This supplies correction coordinates without requiring that the label already occur among guarded candidates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/BankPaperCanonicalRawBroadSurplusAsymptotic.lean#L743-L996

